{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_three_gateway_convergence_failure", "label": "3-gateway mesh fails to converge \u2014 NAT-blocked peer destabilizes the fabric", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/ops-finding-multi-gateway-convergence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_punch_socket_starvation", "label": "Punch-socket starvation on the shared WG listen port", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/ops-finding-multi-gateway-convergence.md", "source_location": "crates/wiremesh-gateway/tests/convergence_matrix.rs", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bounding punch attempt COUNT (T3) is not sufficient: every admitted attempt still opens a transient SO_REUSEPORT socket on :51820 that can intercept an established peer's inbound WG datagrams, so endpoint-level make-before-break is necessary but not sufficient \u2014 the established session itself resets. The defect is architectural: the puncher must not share the WG listen socket."}, {"id": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_peer_set_reapply_endpoint_reset", "label": "Peer-set re-application resets established endpoints", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/ops-finding-multi-gateway-convergence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A newcomer must not break existing tunnels \u2014 make-before-break applies to peer-set updates too. Fixed as T4 plus an incremental add-only apply."}, {"id": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_last_handshake_false_advance", "label": "last_handshake_time false-advance accepted a dead tunnel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/ops-finding-multi-gateway-convergence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Path liveness must require corroborating rx delta, not handshake plus any-rx-once; the boringtun elapsed-vs-absolute handshake-timestamp bug was the real cause (fixed as T2)."}, {"id": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_missing_persistent_keepalive", "label": "No WireGuard persistent_keepalive \u2014 NAT mapping sawtooth", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/ops-finding-multi-gateway-convergence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_relay_packaging_permission_denied", "label": "Relay packaging Finding A \u2014 certdir collision crash-loop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/ops-finding-multi-gateway-convergence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The .deb unit ran User=wiremesh while the enroll binary wrote root-owned 0600 files, and the documented --certdir collided with the gateway's root-only state dir; fixed with a dedicated StateDirectory, postinstall script and chown-when-root."}, {"id": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_relay_sync_authorization_denial", "label": "Relay Sync Finding B \u2014 controller rejected the relay's revocation watch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/ops-finding-multi-gateway-convergence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sync authorized only gateway certs, so the offline denylist never updated post-enrollment; fixed with a revocation-scoped watch_relay carrying revoked_serials only, structurally out of the punch broker."}, {"id": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_revoked_cert_watch_not_severed", "label": "Security follow-up \u2014 RevokeCert does not sever an open control-plane Watch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/ops-finding-multi-gateway-convergence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Watch authorization gates on ROW status, not cert revocation. The relay path is deliberately consistent with the gateway path \u2014 guarding only the relay watch would protect the low-sensitivity surface while leaving the high-sensitivity gateway watch open, which is backwards. A uniform change would contradict rebind.rs's current expectation that revocation surfaces via the denylist."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_three_gateway_convergence_failure", "target": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_punch_socket_starvation", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/ops-finding-multi-gateway-convergence.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_three_gateway_convergence_failure", "target": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_peer_set_reapply_endpoint_reset", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/ops-finding-multi-gateway-convergence.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_three_gateway_convergence_failure", "target": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_last_handshake_false_advance", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/ops-finding-multi-gateway-convergence.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_ops_finding_multi_gateway_convergence_three_gateway_convergence_failure", "target": "docs_research_